county schools likely will not return to  learning in person anytime  soon last night trustees were briefed on  the district's coronavirus response  back in july the board set some strict  requirements for reopening schools  that includes a 5 percent or lower  positivity rate  and a downward trend in cases for 14  days  well a doctor with the southern nevada  health district last night said clark  county is not close to those benchmarks  but he would support the board's  decision to return if they have a plan  for limiting capacity and social  distancing  board members though made it clear  there's no easy answer  would it be more safe for everybody to  keep schools  closed or at least only  partially open um i don't know i just  feel really uncomfortable with this  whole thing  and it doesn't seem like there's a lot  of answers and i really don't like the  answer of  just reopen because it's not going to  get better this year  the school board plans to vote on the  future of in-person learning on november  12th we will of course follow that for  you
 

